{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TraceBlindSector","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.TraceBlindSector","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TraceRealSpectrumComplex"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zero_weight_admits_both_spectra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zero_weight_admits_both_spectra","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceBlindSector.lean#L196-L201","doc":"The same statement in the form the blind sector uses it: a block carrying\nweight zero contributes `0` to the observable for **either** operator, so the\nobservable is consistent with both the elliptic and the hyperbolic one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.spectrum_not_determined_by_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.spectrum_not_determined_by_trace","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceBlindSector.lean#L184-L194","doc":"**A weighted trace does not determine a spectrum.** Two operators sharing\nevery trace the corpus computes can differ in discriminant — one elliptic, one\nhyperbolic. So the eigenphases of a zero-weight block are not constrained by any\nmeasurement, which is what makes the blind sector a place a phase could live\nwithout contradicting anything.\n\nWitness on the invariants: `tr = 0` with `det = 1` (elliptic, `disc = −4`) and\n`tr = 0` with `det = −1` (hyperbolic, `disc = +4`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.blind_dim_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.blind_dim_A3","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceBlindSector.lean#L176-L180","doc":"And the blindness deepens with the nucleus. At `A = 3` the strand count is\n`n = 9`, so the observable sees `C₉ = 4862` of `9! = 362880` dimensions — **98.66 %\nblind**, against 81.67 % at `A = 2`. The visible share is `Cₙ/n! ~ 4ⁿ/n!`, which\nfalls super-exponentially: by `A = 6` it is `7.5·10⁻⁶` %. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.blind_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.blind_dim","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceBlindSector.lean#L172-L174","doc":"**588 of 720 dimensions are invisible to the observable** — 81.7 % of the\nalgebra the binding operator lives in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.visible_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.visible_dim","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceBlindSector.lean#L166-L170","doc":"`∑ d² over the visible blocks = 132 = C₆ = dim TL₆`. Convention D factors\nthrough the Temperley–Lieb quotient, and this is that quotient's dimension\nrecovered from the block list — an arithmetic confirmation independent of the\nnumerically-measured Ocneanu weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.total_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.total_dim","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceBlindSector.lean#L160-L164","doc":"`∑ d² = 720 = 6! = dim H₆` — the Artin–Wedderburn count, so the list is the\nright one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.h6Visible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.h6Visible","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceBlindSector.lean#L155-L158","doc":"Which of them convention D can see: exactly the partitions with at most two\nrows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.h6Dims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.h6Dims","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceBlindSector.lean#L150-L153","doc":"The dimensions of the eleven irreps of `H₆`, in the order\n`(6), (5,1), (4,2), (4,1,1), (3,3), (3,2,1), (3,1,1,1), (2,2,2), (2,2,1,1),\n(2,1⁴), (1⁶)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.blind_sector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.blind_sector","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceBlindSector.lean#L137-L148","doc":"**The observable cannot see a zero-weight block.** If the weights vanish on\n`S`, the weighted sum is identical for any two summands agreeing off `S` —\nwhatever they do on `S`. At `n = 6` under convention D, `S` is the seven\npartitions with more than two rows, and `Δ_bind`'s character there is large\n(`χ_{(3,2,1)} = −9.598`, the biggest of any block) and contributes nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.markov_trace_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.markov_trace_binding","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceBlindSector.lean#L125-L133","doc":"The binding number is the trace of the binding **operator**. Trivial as\nalgebra, and the whole point of the construction: because `tr_M` is linear, the\nsubtraction can be done on the operators instead of on the numbers, and what\ncomes out is an operator whose spectrum the numbers never saw. ","signatureChunk":0}]}